- You are now searching three fields (`name`, `activities`, `location.name`) with this expensive regex.
- If the `Stores` collection grows, this query will become progressively slower, potentially timing out or blocking the server.
- The `activities` field is likely an array. Searching an array field with a regex is even more expensive because MongoDB must check the regex against every element in the array.

