+      if (options.debug) console.debug('run: ' + name);
+      fn.apply(this, args);
+    });
```
**Issue:**
If `fn` throws an error, the RxJS subscription will catch it and log it to the console (in development) or silently fail (in production), depending on the RxJS configuration. The original code would have thrown the error synchronously, which might have been caught by a try/catch block in the caller. This change in error propagation behavior can make debugging harder.

**Fix:**
