      catchError(error => {
        // Handle HTTP errors (e.g., 401, 403)
        console.error('Failed to fetch things:', error);
        return throwError(error);
      })
    );
}
```

### Final Verdict
**Do not merge.** This change is unsafe and will cause crashes in production for any unauthenticated user. It must be refactored to use a proper authentication service and include robust error handling.

